We will build a simple **"Task Manager"** app where you can add tasks and view them.

### Prerequisites
*   Node.js installed (Check via `node -v`).
*   A code editor (VS Code recommended).

---

### Part 1: Project Setup

Create a folder for your project and initialize the backend.

```bash
mkdir task-app
cd task-app
npm init -y
```

---

### Part 2: The Backend (Node & Express)

We will create an API to handle data.

1.  **Install dependencies:**
    ```bash
    npm install express cors body-parser
    ```

2.  **Create the server file:**
    Create a file named `server.js` in the root folder.

    ```javascript
    // server.js
    const express = require('express');
    const cors = require('cors');
    const bodyParser = require('body-parser');

    const app = express();
    const PORT = 5000;

    // Middleware
    app.use(cors()); // Allow React to talk to this server
    app.use(bodyParser.json());

    // Dummy Data (In-memory database)
    let tasks = [
        { id: 1, text: "Learn Node.js", completed: false },
        { id: 2, text: "Build a React App", completed: true }
    ];

    // Routes

    // 1. GET all tasks
    app.get('/api/tasks', (req, res) => {
        res.json(tasks);
    });

    // 2. POST new task
    app.post('/api/tasks', (req, res) => {
        const { text } = req.body;
        if (!text) {
            return res.status(400).json({ error: "Text is required" });
        }

        const newTask = {
            id: tasks.length + 1,
            text: text,
            completed: false
        };

        tasks.push(newTask);
        res.json(newTask);
    });

    // Start Server
    app.listen(PORT, () => {
        console.log(`Server running on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
    });
    ```

3.  **Run the Backend:**
    ```bash
    node server.js
    ```
    *You should see: "Server running on http://localhost:5000"*

